<PolicyLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="Our accessibility commitment and how to report a barrier on the Cloud Peptides site."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    We want this site to be usable by as many people as possible, including people using screen
    readers, keyboard-only navigation, or other assistive technology. We aim to meet the Web Content
    Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA.
  </p>

  <h2>What we've built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Semantic HTML structure with proper headings and landmarks.</li>
    <li>
      Full keyboard navigation, including a "skip to content" link and a focus-trapped mobile menu.
    </li>
    <li>Visible focus indicators on every interactive element — never removed.</li>
    <li>Color-contrast targets checked against WCAG AA on every color pairing we use.</li>
    <li>A dark theme, and full support for "reduce motion" operating-system settings.</li>
    <li>
      Automated accessibility testing (axe-core) as part of our development process, on every core
      page template.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Automated testing catches many issues but not all of them — it can't fully evaluate things like
    the quality of a screen-reader experience end to end. We test manually where we can, but we
    don't yet claim a formal third-party accessibility audit or certification.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If you run into something on this site that's hard to use with assistive technology, please let
    us know — <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with what happened and what page you were on, and we'll
    work to fix it.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
